# Integration contracts

For security-sensitive changes, read the official OWASP `.cursor/skills/security-guidance/SKILL.md` and the appropriate ASVS reference files before coding.

- Never expose Stripe secret keys, Supabase service-role keys or Google OAuth secrets to client code.
- Validate data at all server boundaries; authorize every read/write. Supabase RLS is required for user-accessible tables.
- Stripe fulfillment and subscription status come from signature-verified webhooks, not redirect pages. Make webhook processing idempotent.
- Store minimal personal data. Document retention, privacy impact, and sensitive fields.
- For booking, prevent race conditions and double bookings using database invariants/transactions. Calendar availability reads alone do not reserve a slot.
- Use time-zone-aware timestamps and distinguish events, appointments, class capacity and paid bookings.
- Keep provider-specific integration code behind domain interfaces so we can switch hosts without rewriting business logic.
